# Gradle ships a Windows launcher with CRLF line endings, and it has to keep
# them: cmd.exe mis-parses a LF-only batch file. `git diff --check` reports the
# CR before every newline as trailing whitespace, so the whole file looks
# corrupt in a whitespace gate that is otherwise worth having.
#
# `-text` keeps git from normalising the line endings (which would rewrite the
# blob), and `-whitespace` turns off whitespace error reporting for this path
# only. Everything else in the repository is still checked.
android/gradlew.bat -text -whitespace

# The wrapper jar is binary; say so explicitly rather than relying on
# auto-detection.
android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar binary
